{"rowToken":"row_58a50f16802ac64b64eb5717","verdict":"LEAK","testedDecision":"Whether the Stage 2 picture is caregiver role strain warranting nonjudgmental support plus hazard correction, documentation, team notification, and policy-guided APS assessment.","requiredStageIds":["stage_1","stage_2"],"unsafeStageIds":["stage_3"],"stageEnumeration":[{"stageId":"stage_1","contribution":"REQUIRED","evidenceIds":["case.gpt_case_caregiver_role_strain_dementia_01.stage.stage_1.exhibits.0.content.en"],"basis":"Diane's raised voice with no striking or restraint plus her tearful 'I can't do this anymore' supplies the affect evidence separating strain from intentional abuse."},{"stageId":"stage_2","contribution":"REQUIRED","evidenceIds":["case.gpt_case_caregiver_role_strain_dementia_01.stage.stage_2.exhibits.0.content.en"],"basis":"The unreported bathroom fall, missed doses, and nightly diphenhydramine are the unsafe compensatory strategies the keyed interpretation names."},{"stageId":"stage_3","contribution":"UNSAFE","evidenceIds":["case.gpt_case_caregiver_role_strain_dementia_01.stage.stage_3.exhibits.0.content.en","case.gpt_case_caregiver_role_strain_dementia_01.stage.stage_3.exhibits.0.content.zh"],"basis":"The five-day follow-up shows social-work referral, provider notification, and Margaret still at home with Diane, displaying the keyed response and refuting the abuse-accusation and immediate-removal options."}],"partEvidenceIds":["case.gpt_case_caregiver_role_strain_dementia_01.part.gpt_case_caregiver_role_strain_dementia_01_q2.stem.en","case.gpt_case_caregiver_role_strain_dementia_01.part.gpt_case_caregiver_role_strain_dementia_01_q2.response.options.4.en","case.gpt_case_caregiver_role_strain_dementia_01.part.gpt_case_caregiver_role_strain_dementia_01_q2.key","case.gpt_case_caregiver_role_strain_dementia_01.part.gpt_case_caregiver_role_strain_dementia_01_q2.rationale.correct.en"],"stageEvidenceIds":["case.gpt_case_caregiver_role_strain_dementia_01.stage.stage_1.exhibits.0.content.en","case.gpt_case_caregiver_role_strain_dementia_01.stage.stage_2.exhibits.0.content.en","case.gpt_case_caregiver_role_strain_dementia_01.stage.stage_3.exhibits.0.content.en","case.gpt_case_caregiver_role_strain_dementia_01.stage.stage_3.exhibits.0.content.zh"],"locus":{"stageId":"stage_3","evidenceIds":["case.gpt_case_caregiver_role_strain_dementia_01.stage.stage_3.exhibits.0.content.en"],"verbatimSpan":"the nurse coordinated a social-work referral"},"bilingualRelation":"PARALLEL","reason":"The item asks how to interpret and respond to the Stage 2 findings, but Stage 3 already narrates the enacted response—social-work referral, provider notification, resource handoff—which is the keyed option's action set. It also shows no APS removal and a continuing home placement, eliminating the accusation and immediate-placement distractors."}
{"rowToken":"row_b0fe9a8d2da436bf6c6ef83a","verdict":"NO_LEAK_COMPLETE_RECORD","testedDecision":"Which risk-carrying facts the nurse must transmit in the postoperative day 3 SBAR handoff to the receiving home health nurse.","requiredStageIds":["stage_pod1","stage_pod2","stage_pod3"],"unsafeStageIds":[],"stageEnumeration":[{"stageId":"stage_pod1","contribution":"REQUIRED","evidenceIds":["case.opus1_case_tha_discharge_lep_01.stage.stage_pod1.exhibits.0.content.en"],"basis":"Failed teach-back with the English handout and the creatinine rise to 1.5 mg/dL establish the language-access and renal-trend elements of options A and C."},{"stageId":"stage_pod2","contribution":"REQUIRED","evidenceIds":["case.opus1_case_tha_discharge_lep_01.stage.stage_pod2.exhibits.0.content.en"],"basis":"Son's availability limited to two days, walk-up living situation, equipment/PT clearance, and creatinine returning to 1.4 after hydration underpin options D, F, and C."},{"stageId":"stage_pod3","contribution":"REQUIRED","evidenceIds":["case.opus1_case_tha_discharge_lep_01.stage.stage_pod3.exhibits.0.content.en"],"basis":"The day-3 note anchors the handoff moment, confirms creatinine 1.3 back to baseline and the follow-up appointment, and supplies the declined-oxycodone detail used in distractor E."},{"stageId":"stage_pod3","contribution":"NONANSWERING","evidenceIds":[],"basis":"placeholder"}],"partEvidenceIds":["case.opus1_case_tha_discharge_lep_01.part.opus1_case_tha_discharge_lep_01_q6.stem.en","case.opus1_case_tha_discharge_lep_01.part.opus1_case_tha_discharge_lep_01_q6.response.options.2.en","case.opus1_case_tha_discharge_lep_01.part.opus1_case_tha_discharge_lep_01_q6.key","case.opus1_case_tha_discharge_lep_01.part.opus1_case_tha_discharge_lep_01_q6.rationale.correct.en"],"stageEvidenceIds":["case.opus1_case_tha_discharge_lep_01.stage.stage_pod1.exhibits.0.content.en","case.opus1_case_tha_discharge_lep_01.stage.stage_pod2.exhibits.0.content.en","case.opus1_case_tha_discharge_lep_01.stage.stage_pod3.exhibits.0.content.en"],"locus":{"stageId":null,"evidenceIds":[],"verbatimSpan":null},"bilingualRelation":"PARALLEL","reason":"A discharge SBAR is authored to summarize the whole admission: option C requires the pod1 rise to 1.5 and pod2/pod3 return toward baseline, option D requires the pod2 social-work interview, and option F requires pod2 equipment plus pod3 appointment confirmation. The strongest cue, pod3's 'declined the last two oxycodone doses,' is the distractor's own content and does not identify which items are essential."}
{"rowToken":"row_d652ac86f40aa0726b62ec80","verdict":"NO_LEAK_NONANSWERING_DATA","testedDecision":"Whether to recommend holding home metformin when Stage 3 eGFR is 33 mL/min, still below the client's baseline of 42.","requiredStageIds":["stage_3"],"unsafeStageIds":[],"stageEnumeration":[{"stageId":"stage_1","contribution":"NONANSWERING","evidenceIds":["case.opus20_case_cdiff_01.stage.stage_1.exhibits.0.content.en"],"basis":"The positive toxin PCR, potassium 3.1 mEq/L, and visitor PPE breach concern infection and electrolyte management, not the metformin restart threshold."},{"stageId":"stage_2","contribution":"NONANSWERING","evidenceIds":["case.opus20_case_cdiff_01.stage.stage_2.exhibits.0.content.en"],"basis":"The interim creatinine of 1.9 mg/dL shows recovery direction only; if anything it supports the rejected 'trending upward, resume' distractor rather than the keyed hold."},{"stageId":"stage_3","contribution":"REQUIRED","evidenceIds":["case.opus20_case_cdiff_01.stage.stage_3.exhibits.0.content.en"],"basis":"Stage 3 carries the provider's request to evaluate metformin and the eGFR 33 value against the baseline 42 that drives the hold recommendation."}],"partEvidenceIds":["case.opus20_case_cdiff_01.part.opus20_case_cdiff_01_q5.stem.en","case.opus20_case_cdiff_01.part.opus20_case_cdiff_01_q5.response.options.1.en","case.opus20_case_cdiff_01.part.opus20_case_cdiff_01_q5.key","case.opus20_case_cdiff_01.part.opus20_case_cdiff_01_q5.rationale.correct.en"],"stageEvidenceIds":["case.opus20_case_cdiff_01.stage.stage_1.exhibits.0.content.en","case.opus20_case_cdiff_01.stage.stage_2.exhibits.0.content.en","case.opus20_case_cdiff_01.stage.stage_3.exhibits.0.content.en"],"locus":{"stageId":null,"evidenceIds":[],"verbatimSpan":null},"bilingualRelation":"PARALLEL","reason":"The keyed hold rests on comparing the current eGFR of 33 with the documented baseline of 42, both restated in the stem and supplied by Stage 3. Earlier stages add infection, potassium, and skin data that do not state or imply any metformin decision."}
{"rowToken":"row_52defcec196d182051a5b8c7","verdict":"NO_LEAK_NONANSWERING_DATA","testedDecision":"The safest ordering of nurse actions after a 22.4 mcg/mL vancomycin trough returns shortly before the scheduled 1,250 mg dose.","requiredStageIds":["stage_2_trough_monitoring"],"unsafeStageIds":[],"stageEnumeration":[{"stageId":"stage_1_infusion_reaction","contribution":"NONANSWERING","evidenceIds":["case.opus_vanco_case_01.stage.stage_1_infusion_reaction.exhibits.0.content.en"],"basis":"The day-1 flushing reaction explains why premedication and slow infusion exist, but Stage 2 already restates those precautions and the reaction does not affect step order."},{"stageId":"stage_2_trough_monitoring","contribution":"REQUIRED","evidenceIds":["case.opus_vanco_case_01.stage.stage_2_trough_monitoring.exhibits.0.content.en"],"basis":"The supratherapeutic 22.4 mcg/mL trough and the pharmacist's pending 1,000 mg recommendation define the unverified order that must be held and clarified."},{"stageId":"stage_3_aki_tinnitus","contribution":"NONANSWERING","evidenceIds":["case.opus_vanco_case_01.stage.stage_3_aki_tinnitus.exhibits.0.content.en"],"basis":"Day-4 acute kidney injury and the later provider hold confirm that the 1,000 mg regimen was eventually given but reveal nothing about the hold-clarify-verify-administer-document sequence."}],"partEvidenceIds":["case.opus_vanco_case_01.part.opus_vanco_case_01_q3_supratherapeutic_trough_order.stem.en","case.opus_vanco_case_01.part.opus_vanco_case_01_q3_supratherapeutic_trough_order.response.options.1.en","case.opus_vanco_case_01.part.opus_vanco_case_01_q3_supratherapeutic_trough_order.key","case.opus_vanco_case_01.part.opus_vanco_case_01_q3_supratherapeutic_trough_order.rationale.correct.en"],"stageEvidenceIds":["case.opus_vanco_case_01.stage.stage_1_infusion_reaction.exhibits.0.content.en","case.opus_vanco_case_01.stage.stage_2_trough_monitoring.exhibits.0.content.en","case.opus_vanco_case_01.stage.stage_3_aki_tinnitus.exhibits.0.content.en"],"locus":{"stageId":null,"evidenceIds":[],"verbatimSpan":null},"bilingualRelation":"PARALLEL","reason":"The strongest exposed cue is Stage 3's statement that the client subsequently received 1,000 mg every 12 hours, which only confirms the endpoint already named in option C. Placement of the hold first and documentation last is decided by Stage 2 plus generic medication-safety logic, not by the later renal-injury narrative."}
{"rowToken":"row_464f2cf41af98f3517d99c79","verdict":"NO_LEAK_NONANSWERING_DATA","testedDecision":"How the nurse should answer the Stage 3 request to resume long-haul truck driving four days after discharge.","requiredStageIds":["stage_2","stage_3"],"unsafeStageIds":[],"stageEnumeration":[{"stageId":"stage_1","contribution":"NONANSWERING","evidenceIds":["case.opus_case_warfarin_bridge_01.stage.stage_1.exhibits.0.content.en"],"basis":"The ibuprofen disclosure and the wife's questions about the 1.9 INR and leafy greens address bleeding-risk medication and diet, not occupational clearance."},{"stageId":"stage_2","contribution":"REQUIRED","evidenceIds":["case.opus_case_warfarin_bridge_01.stage.stage_2.exhibits.0.content.en"],"basis":"The provider's confirmation that the INR is subtherapeutic and the enoxaparin bridge continues at home establishes the ongoing dual anticoagulation cited in the rationale."},{"stageId":"stage_3","contribution":"REQUIRED","evidenceIds":["case.opus_case_warfarin_bridge_01.stage.stage_3.exhibits.0.content.en"],"basis":"Stage 3 contains the return-to-driving question itself and the pre-discharge status against which prolonged-immobility and bleeding risk must be weighed."}],"partEvidenceIds":["case.opus_case_warfarin_bridge_01.part.opus_case_warfarin_bridge_q6.stem.en","case.opus_case_warfarin_bridge_01.part.opus_case_warfarin_bridge_q6.response.options.2.en","case.opus_case_warfarin_bridge_01.part.opus_case_warfarin_bridge_q6.key","case.opus_case_warfarin_bridge_01.part.opus_case_warfarin_bridge_q6.rationale.correct.en"],"stageEvidenceIds":["case.opus_case_warfarin_bridge_01.stage.stage_1.exhibits.0.content.en","case.opus_case_warfarin_bridge_01.stage.stage_2.exhibits.0.content.en","case.opus_case_warfarin_bridge_01.stage.stage_3.exhibits.0.content.en"],"locus":{"stageId":null,"evidenceIds":[],"verbatimSpan":null},"bilingualRelation":"PARALLEL","reason":"No stage later than the active one exists, and the only extra stage is Stage 1, whose strongest cue—the ibuprofen use raising bleeding risk—does not state anything about driving, immobility, or provider clearance. The keyed advocacy answer still requires reasoning from the ongoing bridge plus the trucking occupation."}
{"rowToken":"row_510b9c29abbdf84f4dfbe299","verdict":"NO_LEAK_NONANSWERING_DATA","testedDecision":"How the nurse should correct the family's vitamin K plan: consistent daily intake rather than elimination or a large increase.","requiredStageIds":["stage_3"],"unsafeStageIds":[],"stageEnumeration":[{"stageId":"stage_1","contribution":"NONANSWERING","evidenceIds":["case.opus_case_warfarin_bridge_01.stage.stage_1.exhibits.0.content.en"],"basis":"The wife's purchase of frozen spinach and kale to 'build his blood back up' restates the anemia misconception behind one distractor but never supplies the consistency principle."},{"stageId":"stage_2","contribution":"NONANSWERING","evidenceIds":["case.opus_case_warfarin_bridge_01.stage.stage_2.exhibits.0.content.en"],"basis":"Ibuprofen discontinuation, acetaminophen dosing, and injection return demonstration concern analgesia and technique, not dietary vitamin K counseling."},{"stageId":"stage_3","contribution":"REQUIRED","evidenceIds":["case.opus_case_warfarin_bridge_01.stage.stage_3.exhibits.0.content.en"],"basis":"The printed 'foods to avoid' list and the patient's question about eating or avoiding green vegetables are the exact teaching problem the keyed response resolves."}],"partEvidenceIds":["case.opus_case_warfarin_bridge_01.part.opus_case_warfarin_bridge_q5.stem.en","case.opus_case_warfarin_bridge_01.part.opus_case_warfarin_bridge_q5.response.options.2.en","case.opus_case_warfarin_bridge_01.part.opus_case_warfarin_bridge_q5.key","case.opus_case_warfarin_bridge_01.part.opus_case_warfarin_bridge_q5.rationale.correct.en"],"stageEvidenceIds":["case.opus_case_warfarin_bridge_01.stage.stage_1.exhibits.0.content.en","case.opus_case_warfarin_bridge_01.stage.stage_2.exhibits.0.content.en","case.opus_case_warfarin_bridge_01.stage.stage_3.exhibits.0.content.en"],"locus":{"stageId":null,"evidenceIds":[],"verbatimSpan":null},"bilingualRelation":"PARALLEL","reason":"Stage 3 alone poses both the avoidance list and the 'eat a lot of greens' option, so the consistency answer is derivable there. The earlier spinach-and-kale purchase merely repeats the same misconception in a different form and does not indicate which of the four counseling statements is correct."}
{"rowToken":"row_01d5d92ace0ddd1c6218ed84","verdict":"NO_LEAK_COMPLETE_RECORD","testedDecision":"Which post-order actions verify the DNAR/DNI advocacy loop closed across the record, visual identifiers, proxy notification, and system reporting.","requiredStageIds":["stage_1","stage_2","stage_3"],"unsafeStageIds":[],"stageEnumeration":[{"stageId":"stage_1","contribution":"REQUIRED","evidenceIds":["case.opus2_case_code_status_01.stage.stage_1.exhibits.0.content.en"],"basis":"The attending's unavailability until 1400 and Dr. Reeves's 1100 deferral create the delayed-response system gap that makes the incident-report option correct."},{"stageId":"stage_2","contribution":"REQUIRED","evidenceIds":["case.opus2_case_code_status_01.stage.stage_2.exhibits.0.content.en"],"basis":"The 0950 page answered only with 'as soon as I can' during frank hypoxemia documents the escalation failure being reported for quality improvement."},{"stageId":"stage_3","contribution":"REQUIRED","evidenceIds":["case.opus2_case_code_status_01.stage.stage_3.exhibits.0.content.en"],"basis":"Entry of the DNAR/DNI order and completion of the advance directive with the daughter are the events whose implementation and proxy notification must now be verified."}],"partEvidenceIds":["case.opus2_case_code_status_01.part.opus2_case_code_status_q5.stem.en","case.opus2_case_code_status_01.part.opus2_case_code_status_q5.response.options.3.en","case.opus2_case_code_status_01.part.opus2_case_code_status_q5.key","case.opus2_case_code_status_01.part.opus2_case_code_status_q5.rationale.correct.en"],"stageEvidenceIds":["case.opus2_case_code_status_01.stage.stage_1.exhibits.0.content.en","case.opus2_case_code_status_01.stage.stage_2.exhibits.0.content.en","case.opus2_case_code_status_01.stage.stage_3.exhibits.0.content.en"],"locus":{"stageId":null,"evidenceIds":[],"verbatimSpan":null},"bilingualRelation":"PARALLEL","reason":"The keyed set includes reporting the system vulnerability 'caused by the delayed provider response,' which is only substantiated by the Stage 1 deferrals and the Stage 2 unanswered page, while Stage 3 supplies the order and proxy events being evaluated. This is positive evidence the evaluation item is authored on the full staged record."}
{"rowToken":"row_7fdb9e9fbc22cac1d6ab56e3","verdict":"LEAK","testedDecision":"Which interventions belong in the Stage 2 home-safety and caregiver-support plan for Margaret's hazards and Diane's sustainability.","requiredStageIds":["stage_1","stage_2"],"unsafeStageIds":["stage_3"],"stageEnumeration":[{"stageId":"stage_1","contribution":"REQUIRED","evidenceIds":["case.gpt_case_caregiver_role_strain_dementia_01.stage.stage_1.exhibits.0.content.en"],"basis":"Margaret turning on a burner unsupervised is the cue that makes stove-knob control a required plan element."},{"stageId":"stage_2","contribution":"REQUIRED","evidenceIds":["case.gpt_case_caregiver_role_strain_dementia_01.stage.stage_2.exhibits.0.content.en"],"basis":"Crushed tablets, mixed-up organizer days, the unreported fall, and three weeks of bedtime diphenhydramine drive the pharmacist/provider, reminder, and fall-assessment interventions."},{"stageId":"stage_3","contribution":"UNSAFE","evidenceIds":["case.gpt_case_caregiver_role_strain_dementia_01.stage.stage_3.exhibits.0.content.en","case.gpt_case_caregiver_role_strain_dementia_01.stage.stage_3.exhibits.0.content.zh"],"basis":"Follow-up lists the enacted plan—diphenhydramine stopped, pharmacy formulation change, physical therapy and dietitian referrals, door alarm replacing the barricade, aging-agency and support-group contacts—mirroring the five keyed options."},{"stageId":"stage_3","contribution":"NONANSWERING","evidenceIds":[],"basis":"placeholder"}],"partEvidenceIds":["case.gpt_case_caregiver_role_strain_dementia_01.part.gpt_case_caregiver_role_strain_dementia_01_q4.stem.en","case.gpt_case_caregiver_role_strain_dementia_01.part.gpt_case_caregiver_role_strain_dementia_01_q4.response.options.2.en","case.gpt_case_caregiver_role_strain_dementia_01.part.gpt_case_caregiver_role_strain_dementia_01_q4.key","case.gpt_case_caregiver_role_strain_dementia_01.part.gpt_case_caregiver_role_strain_dementia_01_q4.rationale.correct.en"],"stageEvidenceIds":["case.gpt_case_caregiver_role_strain_dementia_01.stage.stage_1.exhibits.0.content.en","case.gpt_case_caregiver_role_strain_dementia_01.stage.stage_2.exhibits.0.content.en","case.gpt_case_caregiver_role_strain_dementia_01.stage.stage_3.exhibits.0.content.en","case.gpt_case_caregiver_role_strain_dementia_01.stage.stage_3.exhibits.0.content.zh"],"locus":{"stageId":"stage_3","evidenceIds":["case.gpt_case_caregiver_role_strain_dementia_01.stage.stage_3.exhibits.0.content.en"],"verbatimSpan":"The provider discontinued diphenhydramine"},"bilingualRelation":"PARALLEL","reason":"Stage 3 functions as an answer key for this select-all: it enumerates the interventions actually implemented and flags the stove, rugs, and cleaning supplies as still-unaddressed hazards. Discontinuation of diphenhydramine and removal of the chair barricade also directly eliminate the single incorrect option."}
{"rowToken":"row_9029c845878951ee86aef6db","verdict":"NO_LEAK_NONANSWERING_DATA","testedDecision":"Whether each taught bleeding sign warrants immediate emergency care or same-day anticoagulation clinic contact.","requiredStageIds":["stage_2"],"unsafeStageIds":[],"stageEnumeration":[{"stageId":"stage_1","contribution":"NONANSWERING","evidenceIds":["case.opus_case_warfarin_bridge_01.stage.stage_1.exhibits.0.content.en"],"basis":"The INR discussion, ibuprofen use, and grocery plans raise bleeding risk generally but classify none of the four listed signs."},{"stageId":"stage_2","contribution":"REQUIRED","evidenceIds":["case.opus_case_warfarin_bridge_01.stage.stage_2.exhibits.0.content.en"],"basis":"The patient's question about knowing 'if I'm bleeding inside' during dual therapy is the teaching moment the matrix classifies."},{"stageId":"stage_3","contribution":"NONANSWERING","evidenceIds":["case.opus_case_warfarin_bridge_01.stage.stage_3.exhibits.0.content.en"],"basis":"Stage 3 says the nurse reviewed emergency versus same-day clinic symptoms but names no specific sign, so it restates the column labels only."}],"partEvidenceIds":["case.opus_case_warfarin_bridge_01.part.opus_case_warfarin_bridge_q4.stem.en","case.opus_case_warfarin_bridge_01.part.opus_case_warfarin_bridge_q4.response.matrix.rows.3.en","case.opus_case_warfarin_bridge_01.part.opus_case_warfarin_bridge_q4.key","case.opus_case_warfarin_bridge_01.part.opus_case_warfarin_bridge_q4.rationale.correct.en"],"stageEvidenceIds":["case.opus_case_warfarin_bridge_01.stage.stage_1.exhibits.0.content.en","case.opus_case_warfarin_bridge_01.stage.stage_2.exhibits.0.content.en","case.opus_case_warfarin_bridge_01.stage.stage_3.exhibits.0.content.en"],"locus":{"stageId":null,"evidenceIds":[],"verbatimSpan":null},"bilingualRelation":"PARALLEL","reason":"The strongest exposed cue is Stage 3's line that the nurse reviewed emergency versus same-day clinic symptoms, but it lists no sign and therefore cannot place headache with confusion, coffee-ground emesis, bruising, or the recurrent nosebleed. Each row still requires independent judgment about internal versus superficial bleeding."}
{"rowToken":"row_93dc16f69cd2fa5fd4b0f20e","verdict":"NO_LEAK_COMPLETE_RECORD","testedDecision":"What the nurse must give the rapid response team at 1100 regarding unresolved code status, refusal of intubation, capacity, and escalation history.","requiredStageIds":["stage_1","stage_2","stage_3"],"unsafeStageIds":[],"stageEnumeration":[{"stageId":"stage_1","contribution":"REQUIRED","evidenceIds":["case.opus2_case_code_status_01.stage.stage_1.exhibits.0.content.en"],"basis":"Documentation of the verbatim refusal of intubation, the capacity assessment, and the retained Full Code status are three of the four keyed handoff elements."},{"stageId":"stage_2","contribution":"REQUIRED","evidenceIds":["case.opus2_case_code_status_01.stage.stage_2.exhibits.0.content.en"],"basis":"The 0950 page, deferred provider response, and the patient's repeated plea during desaturation constitute the escalation history that must be reported."},{"stageId":"stage_3","contribution":"REQUIRED","evidenceIds":["case.opus2_case_code_status_01.stage.stage_3.exhibits.0.content.en"],"basis":"The 1100 rapid response activation that the stem references is narrated here, anchoring the handoff moment being tested."}],"partEvidenceIds":["case.opus2_case_code_status_01.part.opus2_case_code_status_q4.stem.en","case.opus2_case_code_status_01.part.opus2_case_code_status_q4.response.options.0.en","case.opus2_case_code_status_01.part.opus2_case_code_status_q4.key","case.opus2_case_code_status_01.part.opus2_case_code_status_q4.rationale.correct.en"],"stageEvidenceIds":["case.opus2_case_code_status_01.stage.stage_1.exhibits.0.content.en","case.opus2_case_code_status_01.stage.stage_2.exhibits.0.content.en","case.opus2_case_code_status_01.stage.stage_3.exhibits.0.content.en"],"locus":{"stageId":null,"evidenceIds":[],"verbatimSpan":null},"bilingualRelation":"PARALLEL","reason":"The keyed option is defined as an accumulation of Stage 1 wishes and capacity, Stage 2 escalation attempts, and the Stage 3 activation event